WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.090
Our school tried a model to warn us early

2
00:00:04.090 --> 00:00:07.230
about pupils who might need extra help.

3
00:00:07.880 --> 00:00:09.680
It was ninety percent accurate.

4
00:00:10.540 --> 00:00:13.540
Then we noticed it had not warned

5
00:00:13.540 --> 00:00:15.340
us about a single pupil.

6
00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:18.820
Today: how to judge a model by

7
00:00:18.820 --> 00:00:19.780
the mistakes it makes.

8
00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:23.340
Accuracy is the share of cases

9
00:00:23.340 --> 00:00:24.700
the model gets right.

10
00:00:25.390 --> 00:00:28.230
But if only one pupil in ten needs help,

11
00:00:28.690 --> 00:00:31.590
a model that always says no help is

12
00:00:31.590 --> 00:00:33.190
already ninety percent accurate.

13
00:00:33.980 --> 00:00:37.180
Accuracy alone can hide a useless model.

14
00:00:38.410 --> 00:00:40.990
A model can make two kinds of mistake.

15
00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:44.120
A false alarm warns about a

16
00:00:44.120 --> 00:00:45.640
pupil who is fine.

17
00:00:46.390 --> 00:00:49.110
A miss stays quiet about a pupil who

18
00:00:49.110 --> 00:00:51.950
really needs help, and at school a

19
00:00:51.950 --> 00:00:53.950
miss usually costs more.

20
00:00:55.160 --> 00:00:57.280
We count all four results

21
00:00:57.280 --> 00:00:58.740
for one hundred pupils.

22
00:00:59.570 --> 00:01:01.730
Eight were caught, two were missed,

23
00:01:02.270 --> 00:01:04.610
six were false alarms and eighty

24
00:01:04.610 --> 00:01:06.410
four were rightly left alone.

25
00:01:07.720 --> 00:01:09.960
Many models give each pupil a

26
00:01:09.960 --> 00:01:11.580
score from zero to one.

27
00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:13.960
We choose a threshold, and

28
00:01:13.960 --> 00:01:15.260
pupils above it get a warning.

29
00:01:15.900 --> 00:01:18.240
Lower the threshold and you catch more

30
00:01:18.240 --> 00:01:21.060
pupils, but you also raise more false

31
00:01:21.060 --> 00:01:21.520
alarms.

32
00:01:22.940 --> 00:01:25.000
Choosing the threshold is

33
00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:26.460
not a maths question.

34
00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:30.180
A false alarm costs a student a short

35
00:01:30.180 --> 00:01:33.760
chat, while a miss can cost a student a

36
00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:34.120
year.

37
00:01:34.690 --> 00:01:38.450
So the school chose a low threshold, and a

38
00:01:38.450 --> 00:01:40.690
person always checks each warning.

39
00:01:41.990 --> 00:01:42.470
Quick check!

40
00:01:43.080 --> 00:01:46.360
One pupil in ten needs help, and a

41
00:01:46.360 --> 00:01:48.480
model always says no help.

42
00:01:49.010 --> 00:01:50.970
It is ninety percent accurate.

43
00:01:51.830 --> 00:01:53.010
Is it a good model?

44
00:01:54.220 --> 00:01:54.460
No.

45
00:01:55.030 --> 00:01:56.550
It misses every single

46
00:01:56.550 --> 00:01:57.850
pupil who needs help.

47
00:01:58.470 --> 00:02:00.870
Always look at the misses and the false

48
00:02:00.870 --> 00:02:02.910
alarms, not only the accuracy.

49
00:02:04.380 --> 00:02:06.480
In the app, open the threshold lab.

50
00:02:07.130 --> 00:02:09.470
Slide the threshold down and up,

51
00:02:09.630 --> 00:02:11.850
and watch the four boxes of the

52
00:02:11.850 --> 00:02:13.330
confusion matrix change.

53
00:02:14.680 --> 00:02:15.220
Your turn.

54
00:02:15.830 --> 00:02:17.710
What happens when we lower the

55
00:02:17.710 --> 00:02:18.810
threshold for a warning?

56
00:02:20.110 --> 00:02:22.330
We catch more pupils, and we

57
00:02:22.330 --> 00:02:23.570
get more false alarms.

58
00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:27.120
Remember: accuracy can hide misses,

59
00:02:27.660 --> 00:02:29.860
count both kinds of mistake, and let

60
00:02:29.860 --> 00:02:30.940
people choose the threshold.

61
00:02:32.270 --> 00:02:34.490
Try it yourself: keep a rain

62
00:02:34.490 --> 00:02:36.490
forecast for a week, and note

63
00:02:36.490 --> 00:02:37.690
whether it rained each day.

64
00:02:38.250 --> 00:02:40.650
Fill a two by two table and decide

65
00:02:40.650 --> 00:02:42.370
which mistake was worse for you.
